{
  "dom_id": "step-t4836",
  "name": "Writing a Condition for a Point To Be a Local Extremum",
  "problem": "Let's go back to looking at the function $y=f(x)$ that we saw earlier.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/197834de138cb2e05a3af391bbeec1279ad8bfddfb277b881e5e3eeb49bcb73a.png)\n\nThe point $A$ where $x=0$ is a local maximum of $f(x)$ because we can draw an open interval around $x=0$ such that the point $A$ is the highest point on the graph. One such interval is $x\\in (-0.5,0.5),$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/d522b4b0a59ff328399493bc12a770af2d99a1587b2826accb9835d7463ef9ba.png)\n\nEverywhere in this interval, the value of the function is *less than or equal to* $f(0),$ the largest value of the function in this interval. We can write this mathematically as\n\n$\\qquad$ $f(x) \\leq f(0)$ for all $x\\in(-0.5, 0.5).$\n\nSimilarly, the point $B$ where $x=2$ is a local minimum of $f(x)$ because we can draw an open interval around $x=2$ such that the point $B$ is the lowest point on the graph. One such interval is $x\\in (1.5,2.5),$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/e2a92d4217e1eebcc724e48cca273d2e707731ded914207e59fff149b46b4dcc.png)\n\nEverywhere in this interval, the value of the function is *greater than or equal to* $f(2),$ the smallest value of the function in this interval. We can write this mathematically as\n\n$\\qquad$ $f(x) \\geq f(2)$ for all $x\\in(1.5, 2.5).$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-t4836\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n               \n                <div class=\"tutorial\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Writing a Condition for a Point To Be a Local Extremum</span></div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"t4836\">?</div>\n                    </div>                    \n    \n                    <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                  